# Impossible OS user-mode test manifest
# =====================================
#
# Deployed by `make userland` to C:\tests\usermode.manifest.
# Read by the kernel-side launcher in src/kernel/test/test_usermode.c
# (TODO-04 §3 + §4). One filename per line, `#` starts a comment,
# blank lines are ignored. Order in this file is the execution order
# -- the launcher honours it so tests can declare deterministic
# dependencies (e.g. run a smoke first, then subsystem coverage).
#
# Behavior:
#   - First §1 smoke so a broken UTEST harness itself fails loud.
#   - Then §2 (build-validating) syscall stub.
#   - Future §9-§15 binaries append here as they ship.
#
# Binaries not listed here are STILL run (via directory glob) when
# this manifest is absent OR when the §4 UTEST_MANIFEST_MAX cap is
# tripped. The manifest is a priority list, not a restriction list.
#
# To restrict the run to ONE binary, set `utest_filter=test_foo.exe`
# in boot.conf (TODO-04 §4). Glob matching is supported: `test_smoke_*.exe`.

test_harness_smoke.exe
test_syscall.exe
test_faultinject.exe
